FAQ content: When do Stockeld Park Christmas tickets go on sale?







Gold Tickets - (early access) 26th June, (general sale) 27th June
Silver Tickets - (early access) 24th July, (general sale) 25th July
Illuminations - 28th August

Get early access to tickets 24 hours before anyone else by signing up to our mailing list. 









                What do Stockeld Park Christmas tickets include?






            Gold tickets

Christmas Theatre Show
Santa's Grotto
Winter Illuminations 
Six Outdoor Playgrounds 
The Snowflake Maze 

Silver tickets 

Santa's Grotto
Winter Illuminations 
Six Outdoor Playgrounds 
The Snowflake Maze

Illuminations tickets 

Winter Illuminations (entry to the Enchanted Forest and the Snowflake Maze, where the illuminations are located)
Six Outdoor Playgrounds










                What are your opening times during Christmas?






            The Christmas Adventure opens on the 21st November and runs until the 24th December 2026. Winter Illuminations, ice skating, and park activities will remain open until the 3rd January 2027.









                Do I need kids to come to Stockeld Park at Christmas?






            No - Our Winter Illuminations and Ice Skating make for a magical festive date night with your other half. And, they're perfect for a Christmas get together with friends too! 









                Where can I get a discount code for Stockeld Park?






            By signing up to our newsletter, you'll receive exclusive discounts and early ticket releases.









                Is Stockeld Park dog friendly?






            No, unfortunately we don't allow dogs at our adventure park, apart from assistance dogs. Head to our accessibility page to learn more about how we support our guests.









                Is Santa's Grotto an individual or group experience?






            At Stockeld, we don't do group visits to Santa unless specifically requested. All bookings are based on one family meeting Santa at a time.
